cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "UCAS-EDML: target leakage in graduation prediction from administrative records"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying article."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yaghi
    given-names: Samer
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0268-7163"
    affiliation: "University College of Applied Sciences, Gaza, Palestine"
  - family-names: Baraka
    given-names: Rebhi S.
    affiliation: "Islamic University of Gaza, Gaza, Palestine"
version: "2.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sameredu/UCAS-EDML-Graduation-Prediction"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for a study of target leakage in machine-learning
  models that predict higher education graduation from administrative student
  records. Includes the leakage diagnostic, the corrected leakage-free pipeline,
  pre-enrolment prediction and a fairness audit by recorded sex.
keywords:
  - target leakage
  - educational data mining
  - graduation prediction
  - algorithmic fairness
  - reproducibility
